---
import PhoneFrame from './PhoneFrame.astro';
import homeShot from '../assets/screens/home.png';
// Safe-to-Spend is a supporting mechanic, not the wedge (ADR 0004, ADR 0005 Amendment).
// Framed here as what the plan leaves you day to day — never announced as a novelty,
// because it isn't one. The reconciliation ledger lives in Trustworthy.astro, where the
// maths is the subject.
---
<section id="safe-to-spend" class="sts-sec">
  <div class="container grid">
    <div class="copy">
      <p class="eyebrow">What the plan leaves you</p>
      <h2>Once the dates are set, the day-to-day question gets <em class="ever">much smaller.</em></h2>
      <p class="lead">
        Every goal’s date already assumes a certain amount going aside each month. So what’s left
        after that — after the bills that haven’t gone out yet, and the money your goals have
        claimed — is genuinely free. Lysning shows it as one number.
      </p>
      <p class="lead">
        Spend it on dinner or let it ride. Either way the dates you set don’t move, because the
        money holding them up was never in that number to begin with.
      </p>
      <p class="note">
        Plenty of apps show a spendable figure. The difference isn’t the number — it’s that
        ours is what’s left over from a plan you can see, rather than a balance with some
        guesswork taken off.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="art">
      <PhoneFrame
        label="Lysning Safe-to-Spend home"
        src={homeShot}
        alt="Home screen: £897 safe to spend, about £60 a day until 30 Sep, above a £17,919.83 live balance with £16,500 set aside for goals."
      />
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .grid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1.05fr 0.95fr; gap: clamp(32px, 6vw, 72px); align-items: center; }
  .art { display: flex; justify-content: center; }
  .copy .lead + .lead { margin-top: 1rem; }
  .note {
    margin-top: 1.6rem; color: var(--ink-secondary); font-size: 0.95rem;
    max-width: var(--measure); padding-top: 16px; border-top: 1px solid var(--rule);
  }
  @media (max-width: 820px) { .grid { grid-template-columns: 1fr; } .art { order: -1; } }
</style>
